To reproduce the experiments, use the `datoscombinadoslimpios.csv` file as the main input dataset. 
This file already includes the necessary preprocessing steps to align and clean the original DAMADICS data files.

## Preprocessed Dataset File

The file `datoscombinadoslimpios.csv` contains a cleaned and consolidated version of the DAMADICS benchmark data used in this study. 
It was generated by combining the original daily `.txt` files provided in the benchmark, which represent 24-hour recordings of sensor data.

The following preprocessing steps were applied:
- All original files were merged in chronological order according to their recording day and internal timestamp (seconds since midnight).
- The original timestamp column was removed, and a unified time index was created, representing absolute seconds across all days.
- Missing values (NaN) were removed.
- A header row was added with the name of each variable, based on the documentation provided in the benchmark (`damadics-lublin-data-description-v02March2002.pdf`).

This consolidated format was used for easier data handling and analysis throughout the experiments, while preserving the original signal integrity and structure.

Researchers using this file should cite the original DAMADICS benchmark and acknowledge the preprocessing described here.
